module gunbc.required_ci_contract_epoch

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.contract_identity { ContractEpoch }

// THE REQUIRED CI CONTRACT'S DECLARED EFFECTIVE EPOCH, in one place, because both sides of the
// comparison must read the SAME authority or the comparison is between two independently writable
// answers rather than between an observation and a requirement.
//
// WHY THIS IS ITS OWN MODULE AND NOT A ROW IN EITHER CONSUMER. Two modules need this value for
// opposite reasons: gunbc.witness_floor_workflow EMITS it into the workflow the required run
// executes, so the epoch is observable at the exact commit that ran; gunbc.fleet_revision_acceptance
// REQUIRES it, so fleet admission can refuse a contract whose obligations were revised under an
// unchanged name. Putting the value in either consumer would make the other import its peer for a
// single datum and would give the emitting side authority over what the judging side requires --
// which is the layer inversion §3 names, and would also make the epoch trivially self-satisfying.
//
// WHAT BUMPING THIS MEANS, since the value is only as honest as the discipline around it. Bump it
// when the Required CI contract's OBLIGATIONS change materially under an unchanged name: what the
// floor admits, what it refuses, or what a success entitles a consumer to conclude. Do NOT bump it
// for a change in what the contract does internally -- the phase roster is the contract's own
// business, and an identity that moved with the roster would make every added phase a breaking
// change to fleet admission, which is the exact backwards rule this identity's own note forbids.
//
// THE HONEST RUNG, stated so it is not over-read: a cross-epoch admission is MECHANICALLY PREVENTED
// by the production join that compares this required value against the observed one. An UNBUMPED
// material change is not -- nothing here derives materiality, so that half is declared-version
// diligence until a contract-surface digest or a classifier distinguishes material from internal
// change. That distinction is the next-rung trigger for this row, and it is a capability, not an
// artifact: acceptance deriving contract materiality from the contract's own surface.
data required_ci_contract_epoch: ContractEpoch = "2026-09-01.1" as ContractEpoch

// The env member name the workflow authority emits and the exact-commit reader looks up. It is
// declared here beside the value because the KEY and the VALUE are one fact about how this epoch is
// carried: a reader looking up a key the emitter does not write, or an emitter writing a key no
// reader looks up, is the same fork in two directions.
data required_ci_contract_epoch_env_key: NonEmptyStr = "GUNBC_REQUIRED_CI_CONTRACT_EPOCH" as NonEmptyStr
